---
scope: "The DECLARATIVE HARDWARE-ABSTRACTION layer — the code-free schema that binds a physical peripheral (a Grove/STEMMA-QT/Qwiic sensor or actuator on a CH32V*/ESP32* MCU, or a host/network adaptor) to a semantic ComposeBus namespace. It is the INPUT/OUTPUT DUAL of the render-widget surface: a widget declares screen output; a `peripheral:` entry declares physical I/O. Each peripheral is a bus peer — a SENSOR publishes readings, an ACTUATOR subscribes to intent, a TRANSACTIONAL device is driven by commands and emits results — with the MCU firmware owning the driver (complexity down at the leaf) and only semantic state crossing the bus (intent up). It spans the two buses a device inherently has (its private INTERNAL bus + the shared COMPOSEBUS, joined by a declared bidirectional membrane over a pluggable transport incl. CAN), models hierarchical addressing (I2C muxes + GPIO/analog expanders + shift registers as PORT-PROVIDERS), compound peripherals (button matrices, gauge clusters, actuator pin-groups, banks), device configuration/calibration, and the driver as a SIGNED, tiered, fetchable BusStorage artifact. Grounded in three cross-validated sources: the Grove peripheral catalog (docs/hardware/grove-peripheral-cross-section.md), the R503 protocol stress test, and four real ComposeBus PCBs (../../../pcb/boards-overview.lts). Realizes the concept-capture in [SPEC:CXC-HAL]."
audience: "ComposeIO/UX architects; the HAL-declaration parser + per-peer runtime builder; the decoder-registry + driver-VM authors; the PCB/firmware author (CH32V003/CH32V203/ESP32-C3 ports, Grove + Adafruit sockets); the Composer peripheral-palette builder"
boundary: "IN: the `peripherals:` schema ([CXC-HALD-DECLARE]); the nine INTERFACE KINDS + params ([CXC-HALD-KINDS]); topology + hierarchical addressing ([CXC-HALD-TOPOLOGY]) incl. muxes/expanders/shift-registers as PORT-PROVIDERS ([CXC-HALD-EXPANDER]); the `driver` join key ([CXC-HALD-DRIVER]); the sensor/actuator/TRANSACTIONAL role model ([CXC-HALD-ROLE]); the by-physical-quantity semantic vocabulary ([CXC-HALD-NAMESPACE]); COMPOUND peripherals — groups, actuator pin-groups, banks ([CXC-HALD-COMPOUND]); device CONFIGURATION/calibration ([CXC-HALD-CONFIG]); collision/allocation validation ([CXC-HALD-VALIDATE]); code-free local RULES at the leaf ([CXC-HALD-RULES]); the internal↔ComposeBus MEMBRANE over a pluggable transport incl. CAN, + authority-gating ([CXC-HALD-BRIDGE]); the driver as a signed tiered BusStorage ARTIFACT + the VM-floor ([CXC-HALD-DRIVER-DIST]); the ecosystem-mining registry seed ([CXC-HALD-MINE]); the peripheral ASSURANCE class ([CXC-HALD-ASSURANCE]); the MCU-as-peer + PCB port model ([CXC-HALD-MCU]); how the built audio/WLED/NFC slot in ([CXC-HALD-BUILT]); the Composer palette ([CXC-HALD-PALETTE]). OUT: the per-chip register maps / protocol framers themselves (the decoder REGISTRY content, keyed by `driver`); the MCU firmware + the driver-VM implementation; the reactive embedded render tier ([SPEC:CXC-EMBED-REACTIVE]); the render-widget surface (this is its DUAL, RELATED_TO)."
not-this: "Not a driver library — the schema NAMES drivers; the register maps live in a registry it joins to. Not a rewrite of the bus — peripherals publish/subscribe ordinary semantic namespaces. Not pixel/frame transport — a status display gets `display/text`, an LED strip gets `led/color`; raw framebuffers/images/waveforms/templates NEVER cross the bus, and a full scene-rendering display is the RENDER TIER ([SPEC:CXC-EMBED-REACTIVE]), not a driver. Not MCU-only — host/network actuators are the same declaration with an `adaptor` interface. Not a security surface — an `assurance` class keeps peripherals from implying guarantees they can't back (a fingerprint reader here is EXPERIENTIAL/theatrical, not access control)."
depends-on: [SPEC:CXC-HAL, SPEC:CXC-BIND, SPEC:CXC-FLAUTH]
