**Status**: DRAFT v3 for review (David 2026-07-18). Consolidated + hardware-grounded. Folds twelve cross-validated refinements from three converging sources — the Grove catalog, the R503 stress test, and four real ComposeBus PCBs (`../../../pcb/boards-overview.lts`): the nine kinds + `adaptor` ([CXC-HALD-KINDS]); hierarchical addressing + port-providers ([CXC-HALD-TOPOLOGY]/[CXC-HALD-EXPANDER]); the transactional role ([CXC-HALD-ROLE]); `gauge/value`/`motor/position` + structured values ([CXC-HALD-NAMESPACE]); compound peripherals ([CXC-HALD-COMPOUND]); config/calibration ([CXC-HALD-CONFIG]); the pluggable-transport + authority-gated membrane incl. CAN ([CXC-HALD-BRIDGE]); the signed tiered driver artifact + VM-floor ([CXC-HALD-DRIVER-DIST]); the assurance class ([CXC-HALD-ASSURANCE]); and the real-board-anchored leaf model ([CXC-HALD-MCU]). The boards are cited inline as the primary illumination — see [PCB-BOARDS-OVERVIEW].

**Architect — build plan flagged for David's go-ahead (NOT started):** (1) the `peripherals:` PARSER (incl. hierarchical addressing + port-providers + compound + config) + per-peer instantiation; (2) a DECODER REGISTRY keyed by `driver`, seeded with the built pn532/ws281x/audio + a first data-descriptor I2C sensor (bme280) + a first port-provider (mcp23017) to prove both seams; (3) the VALIDATOR ([CXC-HALD-VALIDATE]); (4) the RULES + BRIDGE realization (scope the headless-logic layer to the internal bus + the ComposeApp export/import membrane, incl. a CAN transport shim); (5) the driver-artifact tiers ([CXC-HALD-DRIVER-DIST]) — the data-descriptor interpreter + signing/verify first, the bytecode VM later; (6) the Composer peripheral palette. Suggested first slice: parser + registry(pn532/ws281x/audio + bme280 + mcp23017) + validator + a leaf rule + a host-side ComposeApp export/import, all HOST-side — so the built adaptors become declaration-driven, a muxed/expander I2C bank + a compound gauge parse and validate, and the two-bus flow is demonstrated before firmware/PCB.

**Architect — ratifications flagged:** (1) new node-prefixes `CXC-HALD-` (this spec) — a `CXC-` sub-family; needs a [CONV-PREFIX] row. (2) `[CXC-HALD-DECLARE]` REALIZES `[SPEC:CXC-HAL]` (spec 27, concept-capture); a future pass may fold 27's live concepts in. (3) cross-repo ref to `../../../pcb/boards-overview.lts` — the PCB dir is not (yet) under a spec domain; treat as an external hardware-ground-truth companion, not a domain-namespaced node. (4) the semantic-namespace vocabulary ([CXC-HALD-NAMESPACE]) should graduate into a shared CONVENTION registry (sibling to the widget catalog). (5) `provides:`/port-provider addressing and `actuator_group` are the two genuinely new schema shapes — confirm the syntax before the parser is built.
